;; A sheltered hollow under a stepped roof; a steady lift (columns 4-6)
;; rises from its floor to Q. West of it the homeward shaft (D50) comes
;; down from Q beside the cliff (two tiles thick, columns 0-1) onto a rock
;; mass that fills the room's west side (columns 0-3, rows 6-9). Under its
;; thick roof a low alcove is cut, (1,9)-(2,9), and the rose stone stands
;; as the door at its mouth (3,9), at floor level, like the Hollow's Old
;; Cut; the hole down to E (1,10) is inside. The way home, readable before
;; H5 and open with it: a glider lands on the mass, walks off east, comes
;; down its face to the door and, with H5, in and down. Shut, the stone
;; seals the alcove: from E the hole leads only into it, so nothing climbs
;; past it (the reverse route SYSTEMS' replay found when the shaft was
;; open: wall kicks up E's west wall into the shaft, then the lift).
;; test-cloudstair-homeward floods it.
(room
  region: cloudstair
  at: (7 -1)
  title: "Sheltered Seeds"
  intent: "seed creatures rest in a sheltered hollow below the last grass: a breath"
  bed: (wind 0.3 water 0 air 0.5 drone 0.3)
  light: 1
  sun: 1
  grid:
  ("##  ^^^##################"
   "##  ^^^   ###############"
   "##  ^^^     #############"
   "##  ^^^       ###########"
   "##  ^^^         #########"
   "##  ^^^           #######"
   "####^^^             #####"
   "####^^^                  "
   "####^^^                  "
   "#  o^^^ |  ||  |  | |    "
   "# #######################")
  things: ((seed at: (12 9) count: 3)
           ;; the shaft's rose stone (D50), the door of the alcove: shut,
           ;; the way home is sealed and nothing climbs up the shaft from E;
           ;; with H5 it opens as you come to it, and you walk in and drop
           ;; through the hole inside to E
           (ring-stone at: (3 9) overtone: 5)
           (seed at: (5 5) count: 2))
  decor: auto)
